note /lab/ page structure authored in seeded Omega. Run with the pinned hive-page omc; check.sh feeds the
note captured sources on fds 3, 6 and 7 and every captured byte is escaped by emit before it reaches the page.
text t0 "<article class=\"lab\" id=\"lab\">\n<header class=\"lab-hero\">\n<div class=\"lab-sky\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">OMEGA LAB · NOTHING TO INSTALL</p>\n<h1>Write a kernel.<br><span>Run it in one click.</span></h1>\n<p class=\"lab-lead\">This is a data-parallel kernel in Omega, the language I build for programs written with AI. Press Run and it executes in this tab as WebAssembly, with its result checked element by element. Edit it and press Compile: my compiler builds it on my DGX Spark and sends the WebAssembly back.</p>\n<div class=\"lab-cta\"><a class=\"lab-go\" href=\"#lab-play\">Run it now</a><a class=\"lab-alt\" href=\"#lab-home\">Take it home</a></div>\n<div class=\"lab-overview\">\n<div class=\"lab-side lab-omega\"><p class=\"lab-side-h\">Omega, on this page</p><ul><li>Any modern browser</li><li>The compiler and wasm back end: <span data-bytes=\"omega_tool_bytes\">see record.tsv</span>, in the site repo</li><li>omc build of this kernel: <span data-us=\"omc_program_us\">see record.tsv</span></li></ul></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"lab-fact\">Measured on my DGX Spark at 2026-10-27T00:42:59Z, load1 8.15, on 2 of 20 CPU cores. omc built the Omega kernel and host loop in 1.881 ms, the median of 7 builds. The measurements and commands are in"
text t1 " <a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/captures/record.tsv\">record.tsv</a> · <a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/record.sh\">record.sh</a></p>\n</header>\n<section class=\"lab-section\" id=\"lab-play\">\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">01 / RUN IT</p>\n<h2>The Omega kernel.</h2>\n<div class=\"lab-pair\">\n<div class=\"lab-pane\"><div class=\"lab-pane-h\"><strong>Omega</strong><span>axpy.om · editable</span><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/axpy.om\">Forge</a></div><textarea id=\"lab-src\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" rows=\"20\" aria-label=\"Omega kernel source\">"
text t2 "</textarea></div>\n"
text t3 "</div>\n<div class=\"lab-controls\">\n<label>a <input id=\"lab-a\" type=\"number\" min=\"1\" max=\"1000\" value=\"3\" inputmode=\"numeric\"></label>\n<label>elements <select id=\"lab-n\"><option value=\"1024\">1,024</option><option value=\"65536\">65,536</option><option value=\"1048576\" selected>1,048,576</option><option value=\"4194304\">4,194,304</option></select></label>\n<button id=\"lab-run\" class=\"lab-primary\" type=\"button\">Run in my browser</button>\n<button id=\"lab-compile\" type=\"button\">Compile my edit</button>\n<button id=\"lab-break\" type=\"button\">Break it on purpose</button>\n<button id=\"lab-reset\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>\n</div>\n<p id=\"lab-status\" class=\"lab-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading the prebuilt kernel.</p>\n<p id=\"lab-verdict\" class=\"lab-verdict\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n<dl class=\"lab-results\">\n<div><dt>Omega kernel, WebAssembly, this tab</dt><dd id=\"lab-r-wasm\">not run yet</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Kernel checksum</dt><dd id=\"lab-r-sum\">not run yet</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Kernel throughput</dt><dd id=\"lab-r-rate\">not run yet</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Compile on my Spark</dt><dd id=\"lab-c-server\">press Compile</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Round trip from this tab</dt><dd id=\"lab-c-trip\">press Compile</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Compiler pins</dt><dd id=\"lab-c-pin\">press Compile</dd></div>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">How the check works: for every element the kernel computes y[i] = a·x[i] + y[i] with x[i] = i and y[i] = 2i + 1, and returns the sum of all results. An independent reference computes the same sum to check the result. The page calls run in blocks of at most 999,999 elements, keeping each call within the loop bound. Times are the median of three runs in a worker on your device. Integers only for now: the pinned WebAssembly path does not take f32 yet. Signed integer overflow traps. Break it on purpose changes add to sub so you can watch the check catch it.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lab-section\" id=\"lab-backends\">\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">02 / ONE SOURCE, EVERY BACK END</p>\n<h2>What my compiler actually emitted.</h2>\n<p class=\"lab-intro\">Recorded on my DGX Spark by record.sh, except the WebAssembly, which is whatever this tab is running right now.</p>\n<details class=\"lab-be\" open><summary><strong>WebAssembly</strong><span class=\"lab-tag lab-pass\">runs in this tab</span></summary><p id=\"lab-wasm-meta\" class=\"lab-small\">Loading.</p><pre id=\"lab-wasm\" class=\"lab-code\"></pre><p class=\"lab-small\"><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/public/lab/axpy.wasm\">axpy.wasm on the forge</a></p></details>\n<details class=\"lab-be\"><summary><strong>AArch64</strong><span class=\"lab-tag lab-pass\">ran on the Spark CPU</span></summary><pre class=\"lab-code\">"
text t4 "</pre><p class=\"lab-small\"><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/captures/aarch64.txt\">aarch64.txt on the forge</a></p></details>\n<details class=\"lab-be\"><summary><strong>SPIR-V</strong><span class=\"lab-tag lab-pass\">validated, ran on PoCL (CPU)</span><span class=\"lab-tag lab-not\">GPU: NOT_RUN</span></summary><pre class=\"lab-code\">"
text t5 "</pre><p class=\"lab-small\"><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/captures/spirv.txt\">spirv.txt on the forge</a></p></details>\n"
text t6 "</section>\n<section class=\"lab-section\" id=\"lab-race\">\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">03 / EXECUTION RECEIPTS</p>\n<h2>Where it has run, and where it has not.</h2>\n<div class=\"lab-scroll\"><table class=\"lab-table\">\n<thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>What ran</th><th>Elements</th><th>Time</th><th>Check</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"lab-you\"><td>Your device, this tab</td><td>this kernel, Omega to WebAssembly</td><td data-live=\"n\">press Run</td><td data-live=\"time\">press Run</td><td data-live=\"check\">press Run</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/axpy.om\">kernel</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>DGX Spark, Arm CPU</td><td>this kernel, Omega to AArch64, whole process</td><td>1,048,576</td><td data-us=\"native_run_us\">see record.tsv</td><td>MATCH; sub control fails</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/captures/aarch64.txt\">aarch64.txt</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>DGX Spark, Arm CPU</td><td>this kernel, Omega to SPIR-V on PoCL</td><td>1,000</td><td>not timed</td><td>MATCH</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/captures/spirv.txt\">spirv.txt</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>GB10 GPU</td><td>vector add in asm2 (not this kernel)</td><td>1,048,576</td><td>214,257 ns launch to done</td><td>0 wrong</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/omega-mv/commit/3e3da942ad630035ff773982b1aba89b36ba76d6\">omega-mv SEED-0</a> <code>omega-mv 3e3da942ad630035ff773982b1aba89b36ba76d6</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>GB10 GPU</td><td>hello_gpu float add, kernel from my own builder (not this kernel)</td><td>1,048,576</td><td>947.5 µs GPU</td><td>0 wrong</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/CUDApp/blob/2b4b2b14f1c67473b80878d2eff73b32b3522d54/evidence/l424/hello-chip.log\">CUDApp log</a> <code>CUDApp 2b4b2b14f1c67473b80878d2eff73b32b3522d54</code></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"lab-nr\"><td>GB10 GPU</td><td>this kernel from omc</td><td colspan=\"3\">NOT_RUN: omc has no SASS lowering for it yet</td><td><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/omega-mv\">omega-mv</a></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">These are dated receipts for the named kernels, sizes and machine load. The GB10 runs use driver-loaded signed firmware on DGX OS. The asm2 run shared the machine at load1 61; the hello_gpu run had a quiet window.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lab-section lab-model\" id=\"lab-model\">\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">04 / ASK FOR A KERNEL</p>\n<h2>Let Aien write the next one.</h2>\n<p>Aien is my assistant. It runs on my GB10 and writes Omega in the chat, with the same compile and run buttons you just used.</p>\n<p><a class=\"lab-go\" href=\"/aien/\">Talk to Aien</a> <a class=\"lab-alt\" href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/tree/main/om/allen-page\">source</a></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lab-section\" id=\"lab-home\">\n<p class=\"lab-kicker\">05 / TAKE IT HOME</p>\n<h2>Take it home: not open yet.</h2>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">The take-home is three lines from a clone of this site's repository, which is moving to Interplane, my own forge. Downloads are not open yet, so there is no command here today. On Linux on 64-bit Arm it checks the compiler pins, builds the kernel, runs it, checks against an independent reference, runs the broken control and writes the same axpy.wasm this page runs. Other machines get a plain NOT_RUN and a pointer back here. <a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/blob/main/om/lab-page/run.sh\">Read run.sh first.</a></p>\n"
text t7 "<h3>Start your own kernel repository.</h3>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">One command makes a public repository from my template. Edit kernel.om and the independent reference beside it, push, and GitHub's ubuntu-24.04-arm runner builds your kernel for AArch64 and SPIR-V, runs both (SPIR-V on PoCL, a CPU), and checks every result against the reference. No GPU runs there.</p>\n<div class=\"lab-install\"><pre>gh repo create my-kernel --template aien-dev/omega-kernel-template --public --clone</pre></div>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">omega-kernel-template · passing check (<code>omega-kernel-template CI run 40426781699</code>) · failing control: an overflowing kernel must fail (<code>omega-kernel-template CI run 40426783628</code>)</p>\n<h3>Do not trust my compiler? Rebuild it.</h3>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">The seed challenge rebuilds the Omega seed chain from 408 bytes and must land on the same fixed output. It passes on GitHub's own ubuntu-24.04-arm runner, and its tampered-rung, wrong-value and forged-log controls fail as required. From a fresh full clone of omega-mv main (52eba88) on my Spark it printed CHALLENGE PASS in 1.06 s wall. It is a fixed-output reproducibility match, not general self-hosting and not diverse double compiling. It needs the full history of omega-mv, which is moving to Interplane with the rest of my code; downloads are not open yet. From a full copy of omega-mv:</p>\n<div class=\"lab-install\"><pre>cd omega-mv\nsh seed/challenge/run.sh</pre></div>\n<p class=\"lab-small\"><a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/omega-mv/blob/main/seed/challenge/CHALLENGE.md\">CHALLENGE.md</a> · <code>omega-seed-challenge CI run 40426178383</code> · post your result (<code>omega-seed-challenge issues</code>)</p>\n<h3>The GPU bench kit: kernels withdrawn.</h3>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">On 2026-10-27 I withdrew the bench kit's GPU binaries and encoder pending a clean-room rewrite. The kit ships no kernel and ./run prints NOT_RUN on every GPU. Its board retains three earlier rows, not timed. The kit's own run on real hardware: NOT_RUN.</p>\n<p class=\"lab-small\">omega-gpu-bench: the board and receipts.json live in the aien-dev/omega-gpu-bench repository, which has no public page yet.</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"lab-foot\">Page structure and script generated by seeded Omega: <a href=\"https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/aienos.com/tree/main/om/lab-page\">om/lab-page</a>.</p>\n</article>\n"
text amp "&amp;"
text less "&lt;"
text more "&gt;"
fn emit s view uchar 65536 n ulong to int
pos = ulong 0
start = ulong 0
while lt pos n bound 65536
b = get s pos
if or eq b 38 or eq b 60 eq b 62
if gt pos start
k = write 1 s start sub pos start
if ne k long sub pos start
ret 1
end
end
if eq b 38
k = write 1 amp 0 len amp
if ne k long len amp
ret 1
end
else
if eq b 60
k = write 1 less 0 len less
if ne k long len less
ret 1
end
else
k = write 1 more 0 len more
if ne k long len more
ret 1
end
end
end
start = add pos 1
end
pos = add pos 1
end
if gt n start
k = write 1 s start sub n start
if ne k long sub n start
ret 1
end
end
ret 0
end
fn include fd int to int
buf = new uchar 65536 0
total = ulong 0
while true bound 65536
n = read fd buf 0 len buf
if lt n 0
ret 2
end
if eq n 0
if eq total 0
ret 3
end
ret 0
end
total = add total ulong n
if gt total 1048576
ret 4
end
r = emit buf ulong n
if ne r 0
ret r
end
end
ret 5
end
fn main to int
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t0 bound 65536
n = write 1 t0 pos sub len t0 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t1 bound 65536
n = write 1 t1 pos sub len t1 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
r = include 3
if ne r 0
ret r
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t2 bound 65536
n = write 1 t2 pos sub len t2 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t3 bound 65536
n = write 1 t3 pos sub len t3 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
r = include 6
if ne r 0
ret r
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t4 bound 65536
n = write 1 t4 pos sub len t4 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
r = include 7
if ne r 0
ret r
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t5 bound 65536
n = write 1 t5 pos sub len t5 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t6 bound 65536
n = write 1 t6 pos sub len t6 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t7 bound 65536
n = write 1 t7 pos sub len t7 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
ret 0
end
